Resolves #74 
Fits with the work done in https://github.com/ChainSafeSystems/ssz-js/pull/28 

Each `type` and `interface` declaration now has a corresponding piece of data, named identically, that should exist at runtime.
This will let us serialize objects like so:
```typescript
let x: BeaconBlock = {
  ...
};
serialize(x, BeaconBlock);
```
The first reference to BeaconBlock is the typescript interface, which disappears in the compiled javascript.
The second reference is a variable, existing in the compiled javascript, that fulfils the requirements of a ssz "type" (eg: is either an Array, a string, or an object with a `fields` attribute with the desired shape, in this case, mostly objects with `fields`)

