**Motivation**

Refactor our current Lightclient library + Lightclient server that supports it to:
1. Track head, instead of just latest finalized checkpoint. Implements https://github.com/ethereum/consensus-specs/pull/2746
2. Lightclient server capable of generating valid updates without access to state caches, only the postState after importing a block

Closes https://github.com/ChainSafe/lodestar/issues/3207

## Routes description

There are three services that a lightclient server can provide. This PR implements all three but each node or backed may choose to support some of them

### Committee sync provider

**getCommitteeUpdates**

Returns an array of best updates in the requested periods within the inclusive range `from` - `to`. Best is defined by (in order of priority): (1) Is finalized update, (2) Has most bits, (3) Oldest update

```
GET eth/v1/lightclient/committee_updates?from&to

returns altair.LightClientUpdate[]
```

**getSnapshot**

Fetch a snapshot with a proof to a trusted block root. The trusted block root should be fetched with similar means to a weak subjectivity checkpoint. Only block roots for checkpoints are guaranteed to be available.

```
GET /eth/v1/lightclient/snapshot/:blockRoot

returns {
  header: phase0.BeaconBlockHeader;
  currentSyncCommittee: altair.SyncCommittee;
  // TODO: Not really necessary since it can be fetched with an update
  nextSyncCommittee: altair.SyncCommittee;
  /** Single branch proof from state root to currentSyncCommittee parent */
  syncCommitteesBranch: Uint8Array[];
}
```

### Head update provider

New SSE event type `lightclient_update`. Emitted at least once per unique header seen signed by a valid sync committee. Provider may choose to send multiple events for the same header if a syncAggregate with more participation is found. Providers should throttle events and only send updates when a syncAggregate is sufficiently better, i.e. at least 16 new participants.

```
emits {
  type: `lightclient_update`,
  message: {
    syncAggregate: altair.SyncAggregate;
    header: phase0.BeaconBlockHeader;
  }
}
```

### State proofs provider

Returns a multiproof of `paths` at the requested `stateId`. The requested `stateId` may not be available. Regular nodes only keep recent states in memory.

```
GET /eth/v1/lightclient/proof/:stateId?paths

returns ArrayBuffer, serialized tree offset multiproof
```

